Subject: [PATCH v2 0/2] wifi: iwlwifi: ptp: fix race condition in PTP removal

Fix a race condition in both iwl_mvm_ptp_remove() and
iwl_mld_ptp_remove() where cancel_delayed_work_sync() is called too
late, allowing the delayed work to observe partially cleared PTP state
during teardown.

Changes since v1:
- Split into two patches, one per sub-driver, as suggested by
  Simon Horman.
- Removed incorrect claim about work re-arming making the race worse,
  as pointed out by Miri Korenblit.

Claude (2):
  wifi: iwlwifi: mvm: fix race condition in PTP removal
  wifi: iwlwifi: mld: fix race condition in PTP removal

 linux/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/mld/ptp.c | 2 +-
 linux/drivers/net/wireless/intel/iwlwifi/mvm/ptp.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

